# Line-ending policy.
#
# Normalize every text file to LF, both in the repository and in the working
# tree. This repo had no policy until 2026-07-29, and the result was a slow
# divergence: core/autopipette.py was uniformly CRLF from its first commit in
# 2024 (the src/ refactor carried the endings across to the new path),
# core/coordinate.py likewise, plus several single-line __init__.py files.
# A CRLF file makes every edit to it produce a whole-file diff, which buries
# the actual change under hundreds of lines of ending churn.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content and leave it alone, so this
# stays safe if binary assets are ever tracked again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are read by cmd.exe, which requires CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
